    },
    {
      "text": "As-cast HfMoTaTiZr has a density of 10.21 g cm−3.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "HfMoTaTiZr has high strength at room temperature.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions",
        "PMC7513042::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "HfMoTaTiZr retains high strength at elevated temperatures, including approximately 1000 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions",
        "PMC7513042::web::001::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "A small boron addition introduced through powder metallurgy will reduce the density of HfMoTaTiZr.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A small boron addition will not sacrifice the room-temperature mechanical properties of HfMoTaTiZr.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A small boron addition will not sacrifice the elevated-temperature mechanical properties of HfMoTaTiZr up to 1000 °C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boron addition to HfMoTaTiZr will form boride precipitates.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The boride precipitates will refine the grain structure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grain refinement caused by boride precipitation will improve the alloy's strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The lower atomic mass of boron relative to Hf, Mo, Ta, Ti, and Zr will lower the alloy density.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The boron-modified alloy will have improved strength relative to as-cast HfMoTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed performance range extends from room temperature to 1000 °C under tensile loading.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed performance range extends from room temperature to 1000 °C under compressive loading.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Refractory high-entropy alloys can exhibit high melting temperatures, elevated-temperature strength, thermal stability, and resistance to softening.",
